NNAAMMEE
     rruumm — Ralink Technology USB IEEE 802.11a/b/g wireless network driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee eehhccii
           ddeevviiccee uuhhccii
           ddeevviiccee oohhccii
           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee rruumm
           ddeevviiccee wwllaann
           ddeevviiccee wwllaann__aammrrrr

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_rum_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rruumm driver supports USB 2.0 and PCI Express Mini Card wireless
     adapters based on the Ralink RT2501USB and RT2601USB chipsets.

     Ralink PCI Express Mini Card adapters show up as normal USB 2.0 devices
     and are thus handled by the rruumm driver.

     The RT2501USB chipset is the second generation of 802.11a/b/g adapters
     from Ralink.  It consists of two integrated chips, an RT2571W MAC/BBP and
     an RT2528 or RT5226 radio transceiver.

     The RT2601USB chipset consists of two integrated chips, an RT2671 MAC/BBP
     and an RT2527 or RT5225 radio transceiver.  This chipset uses the MIMO
     (multiple-input multiple-output) technology with multiple antennas to ex‐
     tend the operating range of the adapter and to achieve higher throughput.

     All chips have hardware support for WEP, AES-CCM, TKIP, and Michael cryp‐
     tographic operations.

     rruumm supports ssttaattiioonn, aaddhhoocc, aaddhhoocc--ddeemmoo, hhoossttaapp, and mmoonniittoorr mode opera‐
     tion.  Only one virtual interface may be configured at any time.  For
     more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

